      "reduction": "If p outside S divides n or n-1, it divides neither 6H nor the other two consecutive factors. Valuations imply 3 divides v_p(n) or v_p(n-1), respectively. Thus their unique positive cube-free cores A,B are supported on S and coprime.",
      "cardinality_reason": "Each prime has five placements: absent, exponent 1 or 2 in A, or exponent 1 or 2 in B. Swapping A,B has only the fixed pair (1,1), which has no solution in positive cubic bases. Bennett's theorem applied to |A x^3-B y^3|=1 gives at most one positive base pair per remaining unordered core pair; n is the larger of the two terms.",
