      "full_auxiliary_tuple_finiteness": "Also impose 3n<r<10n/3. For each n there are floor((n-1)/3) integer choices of r, finitely many positive H dividing n-2, and at most one T for each n,H,r. If gcd(H,T)=1, n,r uniquely determine H=A0/g and T=r^3/g, where A0=binomial(n,3), g=gcd(A0,r^3). Without a bound on r, the first-index bound alone does not give finiteness of all auxiliary tuples.",
